WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.540
Attention, gorehounds: 2019 was a year that
brought us plenty of sinister thrillers and

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:10.440
chillers, so we thought we'd point out a few
creepshows that really demand your attention.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:15.740
Get ready to scream your heart out, because
these are the most disturbing movies of 2019.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:21.100
It's easy to forget now, but just a few short
years ago, no one really knew who Robert Eggers

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:21.600
was.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:26.820
That changed overnight in 2016 upon the release
of the nerve-shattering Gothic folktale The

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:30.680
Witch, a film that comes highly recommended
for fans of arthouse horror.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.140
After The Witch, fans were eager to see what
Eggers would conjure up next, including actors

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:37.160
Willem Dafoe and Robert Pattinson.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:41.920
In fact, they both reportedly reached out
to Eggers and expressed interest in jumping

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.380
on his next project, whatever that might be.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:48.711
Perhaps they regretted the decision upon arriving
on the set of The Lighthouse, as the film's

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:52.220
icy shoot in Nova Scotia was reportedly a
challenging one.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:55.900
And make no mistake: The Lighthouse is an
extremely challenging film.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:59.460
"I'm damn well wedded to this 'ere light."

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:03.030
We'll keep our lips sealed on all the major
twists and turns of the plot, because the

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.840
less you know going in, the better.

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:09.320
We will say that this is a story about a pair
of lighthouse keepers who are doing whatever

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:14.380
they can to stay sane on an increasingly mystifying
New England island in the 1890s.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:18.140
Eggers' latest is undoubtedly one of the weirdest
films of 2019.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:20.320
It may also be one of the best.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:25.080
Todd Phillips' dark, stylish Joker finally
gives everyone's favorite supervillain an

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.920
origin story, and a highly disturbing one
at that.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:32.940
In a standout performance that's already drawing
award nominations, Joaquin Phoenix plays Arthur

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:36.620
Fleck, a social outcast who suffers from narcissistic
delusions.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:40.740
All too soon, those delusions give way to
horrific bursts of violence.

00:01:40.749 --> 00:01:45.009
The film is arguably even darker than any
installment of Christopher Nolan's Dark Knight

00:01:45.009 --> 00:01:50.220
trilogy, calling to mind gritty Martin Scorsese
classics like Taxi Driver and The King of

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:50.720
Comedy.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:00.460
There's no arguing that Phillips' tale of
a deranged stand-up comic is hopelessly bleak…and

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:04.120
critics spilled gallons of ink writing about
the film's excessive violence.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.600
But perhaps the most disturbing aspect of
Joker is how it succeeds in holding up a funhouse

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.600
mirror to our own troubled times.

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:14.659
Beneath all the greasepaint, the story of
Arthur Fleck is one you wouldn't be surprised

00:02:14.659 --> 00:02:16.190
to see on the evening news.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:19.100
It's a timely cautionary tale, and it hits
hard.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:25.840
In the summer of 2018, Ari Aster unleashed
the unholy horror film Hereditary upon unsuspecting

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:26.340
audiences.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:30.819
And in the summer of 2019, he delivered his
latest experiment in terror.

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:35.080
The fact that Midsommar is mostly set in broad
daylight certainly doesn't detract from the

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:35.580
horror.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:38.380
In fact, in several key scenes, it is the
horror.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:43.120
According to Aster, Midsommar is just a small
film about an unhealthy relationship that

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.230
goes up in flames.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.740
And that's an apt description, at least on
paper.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:51.750
The doomed couple in question visits a Swedish
village's mid-summer festival.Their adventure

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:55.939
eventually turns into a full-fledged waking
nightmare that gives The Wicker Man a run

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:56.700
for its money.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:01.180
Soon enough, they find themselves hopelessly
adrift in the darkest margins of the occult.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:04.879
We'll go ahead and say it: This is folk horror
at its most folked-up.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:05.800
"What is it?"

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.420
"It has special properties."

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:12.140
"What am I going through?"

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:16.660
Of course, Midsommar is a "breakup movie"
only in the way that Hereditary is a "family

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:20.880
drama," and rest assured, every evil under
the sun is on full display here.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:24.880
If you've yet to see the film, you should
know that it's often unbearably gory.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:30.580
Brace yourself for plenty of shocking sights
that you simply can't unsee, popcorn not included.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:34.060
This just might be the scariest, most hallucinatory
film of the year.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.820
Consider yourself warned.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:41.180
With Depraved, underground filmmaker Larry
Fessenden gives us a modern-day retelling

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.780
of the Frankenstein story.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:47.100
The plot is a very familar one: A demented
doctor cobbles together several stray body

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.980
parts to give life to an undead something-or-other.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:55.200
Rest assured, this film is fueled by enough
blood and gore to satisfy even the most discerning

00:03:55.200 --> 00:04:01.011
horror fan, but thanks to deeply human characters
and an inventive and insightful script, Depraved

00:04:01.011 --> 00:04:04.269
is far more nuanced and affecting than you
might expect.

00:04:04.269 --> 00:04:06.900
"In my dreams I'm someone else."

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:11.780
"I owe you something like a normal life."

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:15.860
In this impressively twisted film, even the
noblest intentions can be corrupted…and

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:18.500
men and monsters are often one in the same.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:22.960
One part monster movie, one part character
drama, Depraved explores heavy themes like

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:27.870
post-war trauma and mental illness…but it
remains first and foremost a horror story.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:29.280
A really messed-up one.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.380
Two years have passed since Andy Muschietti
unleashed It: Chapter One on an unsuspecting

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:34.880
public.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:38.800
The film certainly succeeded in scaring the
bejeezus out audiences.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:42.760
It also scared up almost $700 million worldwide
at the box office.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:47.289
Suffice to say, expectations were high for
Chapter Two of this monstrously frightening

00:04:47.289 --> 00:04:48.040
clown epic.

00:04:48.289 --> 00:04:52.600
And we're here to tell you that, yes, It:
Chapter Two is every bit as unsettling as

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:53.360
its predecessor.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:57.970
Bill Skarsgård's absolutely mental take on
Pennywise is still very much the star of the

00:04:57.970 --> 00:05:02.069
show, though he's got some stiff competition
thanks to Bill Hader and Jessica Chastain,

00:05:02.069 --> 00:05:04.530
both of whom turn in powerhouse performances.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:09.810
It: Chapter Two definitely delivers the unbridled
terror that you so desperately crave, and

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:14.080
it amps up the emotional stakes at every turn,
leading to quite a gut-punch of an ending.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:18.380
"For twenty-seven years, I craved you.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:20.820
I missed you."

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:25.820
It's that rare sort of horror film that aims
to shock you and pull at your heartstrings,

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:27.020
and it succeeds brilliantly.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:34.400
Set in Paris in the summer of '79, Yann Gonzalez's
Knife + Heart tells the story of Anne, a filmmaker

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.980
who specializes in arty adult films of the
all-male persuasion.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:42.560
But just as Anne begins her most ambitious
film to date, the members of her troupe start

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:44.040
getting killed off one by one.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:48.699
She suddenly finds herself smack dab in the
middle of a twisted, heartbreaking mystery

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:51.060
that effectively turns her whole world upside-down.

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:56.940
Gonzalez delivers a LGBTQ-centric, truly unique
slasher that pulls no punches.

00:05:56.949 --> 00:06:01.009
It's certainly not for the squeamish, but
adventurous horror fans will definitely want

00:06:01.009 --> 00:06:01.740
to take a look.

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:07.280
Wounds tells the story of a cocksure French
Quarter bartender named Will, played by Armie

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:07.780
Hammer.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:11.820
After he takes home a phone that was left
at his bar, his life begins to get a whole

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:12.400
lot weirder.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:16.720
And when he starts texting the stranger on
the other end, and exploring the highly unsettling

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:20.580
contents of the phone itself, things take
a turn for the truly terrifying.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:25.160
As Will and his girlfriend Carrie, played
by Dakota Johnson, start to unravel the mystery

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:30.050
behind the mysterious smartphone, the film
plunges us deeper into a devilish and depraved

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:33.800
narrative that owes as much to David Cronenberg
as it does to H.P.

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:34.300
Lovecraft.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.400
And we don't make those comparisons lightly.

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:41.200
"There was a ritual."

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:46.920
Based on a bizarre and macabre true story,
Lords of Chaos revolves around a seriously

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:51.600
troubled Norwegian teen who called himself
Euronymous and created what he called "true

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:53.680
Norwegian black metal" with his band Mayhem.

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:58.440
In attempting to bring Mayhem to the masses,
Euronymous and his pals engaged in a wave

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:01.960
of shocking publicity stunts that shook Norway
to its very core.

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:06.400
Mayhem's live shows soon became the place
to see severed pigs' heads, fire-breathing

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:09.080
maniacs, and bloody acts of self-mutilation.

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:14.520
As Euronymous and his crew continue to push
one another, the lines between "act" and "reality"

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:17.640
dissolve, paving the way for arson, violence,
and death.

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:22.280
Lords of Chaos tells a story that feels way
too strange to be true, but it's entirely

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:23.260
based in fact.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:28.010
For his part, director Jonas Åkerlund allows
the increasingly grisly tale to speak for

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:32.659
itself, and he seems to take no particular
delight in presenting the most shocking aspects

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:33.720
of the case at hand.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:38.540
Ultimately, this is haunting biographical
drama about artistic ambition run amok.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:44.220
Add Joe Begos' beastly flick Bliss to the
list of vampire tales reclaiming the genre's

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:48.460
menacing grandeur— even if the word "vampire"
is never actually uttered in the film.

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:53.419
Set among the venomous vistas of modern-day
Los Angeles, Bliss finds a tragically self-centered

00:07:53.419 --> 00:07:57.860
painter stuck in a maddening creative block,
and in debt to some serious shakers in the

00:07:57.860 --> 00:07:59.360
superficial L.A. art world.

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:04.020
In desperate need of inspiration, she turns
to a powerful hallucinatory drug, and with

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:08.629
a little help from a soulless gal-pal, she
quickly spirals into a blood-soaked nightmare

00:08:08.629 --> 00:08:10.800
of lust, death, and, yes, creation.

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:13.020
"I don't know, something came over me.

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:15.509
And it all just started pouring out of me.

00:08:15.509 --> 00:08:16.740
I don't even remember doing it."

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:21.620
The results are spellbindingly sick and twisted,
and unbelievably gory to boot.

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:27.560
Set in Mexico amid the turmoil of the country's
violent drug wars, Issa López's pitch-black

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:32.480
fantasy Tigers Are Not Afraid tells the story
of a little girl named Estrella, whose mother

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:34.020
has mysteriously disappeared.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:38.079
One day, to soothe Estrella after gunfire
is heard outside her classroom, a teacher

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:42.440
gives her three pieces of chalk and says that
they can magically grant her three wishes.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:46.940
Accompanied by a band of fellow orphans, Estrella
adjusts to the perpetual dangers of her new

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:51.000
life and comes to realize that those three
wishes may actually be real.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:53.780
Of course, wishes rarely come true in the
way you expect.

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:58.400
The film is a pitch-perfect, relentlessly
bleak chiller that's as insightful as it is

00:08:58.400 --> 00:08:58.900
creepy.

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:03.520
Edgy, emotional, and deeply moving,Tigers
Are Not Afraid will linger in your head long

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:04.820
after the credits roll.

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:09.480
Some people might not even consider Amanda
Kramer's Ladyworld a movie at all.

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:14.860
It's more of an experimental mood piece about
the fragility of human nature and social structures.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:18.630
After being cut off from the world in the
wake of an unknown natural disaster, a group

00:09:18.630 --> 00:09:21.100
of teenage girls are going positively mad.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:26.140
The film borrows heavily from William Golding's
1954 novel Lord of the Flies, essentially

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:30.980
moving the plot from an isolated island paradise
to the suffocating confines of an apartment.

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:35.500
Rest assured, you can look forward to plenty
of backstabbing and torture, both of the emotional

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:36.840
and physical variety.

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:42.240
"You are a bad leader, and we were never friends."

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:46.589
The claustrophobic photography and wildly
offbeat sound design is bound to keep viewers

00:09:46.589 --> 00:09:47.620
very much on edge.

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:52.471
Featuring a stellar ensemble cast, this film
is definitely its own beast, and that beast

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:53.780
has one hell of a bite.

00:09:54.720 --> 00:09:59.720
It's safe to say that Zach Lipovsky and Adam
B. Stein's outrageous sci-fi film Freaks is

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:01.800
unlike anything you've ever seen before.

00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:06.720
And take our word for it: This film has plenty
of surprises in store for you, so do your

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:09.300
best to avoid any spoilers before giving it
a look.

00:10:09.589 --> 00:10:12.720
Think you already have a good sense of what
Freaks is all about because you watched the

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:13.220
trailer?

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:13.720
Think again.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:18.320
Freaks is the story of a bold little girl,
played by newcomer Lexy Kolker, who's been

00:10:18.339 --> 00:10:22.420
raised in captivity by her overprotective
father, played by Emile Hirsch.

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:25.992
When she tries to make a break for it, she
soon discovers that the world isn't at all

00:10:25.992 --> 00:10:27.050
what she thought it was.

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:30.940
In fact, it might be a far more dangerous
place than she ever could've imagined.

00:10:31.140 --> 00:10:33.260
"You could buy any flavor you wanted with
that."

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:33.880
"Really?"

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:36.460
"Yeah, come around back.

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:37.860
Come inside.

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:40.140
Taste any flavor you want."

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:42.620
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:45.860
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
films are coming soon.

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:50.180
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

